course: dictionary
lesson: 4548
title: One word, many meanings: heat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Heat can be a noun or a verb, and it can mean different things in different sentences. Look at the words around it to find the meaning that fits. «The heat of the day made the path shimmer.» Here heat means the hottest part of the day.
explain: As a verb, heat is an action. «Heat the soup slowly on the stove.» To heat something is to make it warmer or hot. The verb changes its form: heats, heated, heating.
explain: Sometimes heat is a round of a race. «Sam won his heat and went through to the final.» Here a heat is one early race, and the winners go on to the final. The clue words race and final show you which meaning fits.
fact: Heat means warmth, the feeling of being hot.
fact: Heat is energy that moves from hot things to cooler things.
fact: To heat something means to make it warmer or hot, as in «heating soup».
fact: A heat is one early round of a race, and a heatwave is many very hot days.
fact: «Mercury's daytime surface reaches about 430 degrees Celsius, hot enough to melt lead», but at night it falls to about minus 180 because it has almost no atmosphere to keep heat in.
exercise: «The heat of the day made the path shimmer.» What does heat mean here? | A round of a race | *The hottest part of the day | A cold drink
exercise: «Heat the milk gently, then add the sugar.» What does heat mean? | To cool down | *To make something warmer | Warmth in the air
exercise: «Sam won his heat and went through to the final.» What is a heat in this sentence? | *An early round of a race | A flask that keeps drinks warm | Central heating in a house
test: «A heatwave hit the town for three weeks.» What does heatwave mean? | A race to the final | One cold, wet day | *Many very hot days in a row
test: Which phrase means the hottest part of the day? | *The heat of the day | Central heating | Heat up
exam: Which sentence uses heat as a verb? | Central heating keeps the house warm | The heat was too much for the runners | *Heat the pan before you add the oil
